WEBVTT

00:00:00.267 --> 00:00:02.833
Every gap now has a price and a date.

00:00:02.833 --> 00:00:07.600
Now the market talks, and you hear it
first. Signals turns funding rounds,

00:00:07.600 --> 00:00:11.867
hiring pushes and buying behaviour
into scored, evidenced events,

00:00:11.867 --> 00:00:14.833
and only verified ones reach your sellers.

00:00:14.867 --> 00:00:18.533
By the end you'll read the
feed, clear the review queue,

00:00:18.533 --> 00:00:21.733
and set the gate that decides what counts.

00:00:21.733 --> 00:00:25.767
A signal is a dated event about an
account or a person, with a class,

00:00:25.767 --> 00:00:27.700
a weight and evidence.

00:00:27.733 --> 00:00:32.167
Mia's rep sees a funding alert and
calls the account that morning.

00:00:32.167 --> 00:00:34.867
The alert was about a
company with a similar name.

00:00:34.867 --> 00:00:40.600
A feed nobody verified teaches reps
to ignore the feed. A gate fixes that.

00:00:40.667 --> 00:00:42.267
First, where signals come from.

00:00:42.267 --> 00:00:46.333
Your own systems: website tracking,
forms, CRM lifecycle changes,

00:00:46.333 --> 00:00:48.500
mailbox replies, bookings
and product events.

00:00:48.500 --> 00:00:51.667
Server side ones are
verified automatically.

00:00:51.667 --> 00:00:54.700
Then the outside world: looot
web research for funding,

00:00:54.700 --> 00:00:57.167
hiring and expansion,
plus intent topic surge.

00:00:57.167 --> 00:01:00.000
Market events have no live provider yet.

00:01:00.033 --> 00:01:01.633
Second, how a signal is weighed.

00:01:01.633 --> 00:01:04.833
Each has a class: buying,
growth, risk or other.

00:01:04.833 --> 00:01:07.900
Its weight comes from the
signals model, fades with age,

00:01:07.900 --> 00:01:10.300
and is scaled by its verification status,

00:01:10.300 --> 00:01:12.700
so a disputed signal counts for less.

00:01:12.700 --> 00:01:15.500
A kind the model doesn't
list gets a default weight.

00:01:15.500 --> 00:01:18.233
The total is held between
a floor and a ceiling,

00:01:18.233 --> 00:01:19.800
so no single burst takes over.

00:01:19.833 --> 00:01:23.433
Now read the feed. In the
console: CRM, Signals, Feed.

00:01:23.433 --> 00:01:26.733
Open a signal for its evidence sheet:
the source link, the matched text,

00:01:26.733 --> 00:01:28.767
the confidence and the provider.

00:01:28.767 --> 00:01:32.133
Company and contact pages show only
what a seller is allowed to see.

00:01:32.133 --> 00:01:35.400
Or ask your agent: "Surge
report for this week".

00:01:35.467 --> 00:01:38.033
Third, the gate, the
setting that matters most.

00:01:38.033 --> 00:01:40.767
Off: every signal counts
except retracted ones.

00:01:40.767 --> 00:01:44.133
Seller surfaces: unverified
signals still count toward scores,

00:01:44.133 --> 00:01:47.833
but never reach a seller. Strict:
only verified signals count,

00:01:47.833 --> 00:01:50.833
and third party signals
wait in the Review queue.

00:01:50.833 --> 00:01:53.567
Existing organizations start
Off. New ones start Strict.

00:01:53.567 --> 00:01:55.900
You set the mode on the Signals page.

00:01:55.967 --> 00:01:59.300
In Strict mode the Review
queue is your morning chore.

00:01:59.300 --> 00:02:02.233
In the console: CRM,
Signals, Review queue.

00:02:02.233 --> 00:02:06.833
Open a signal, read the evidence, then
verify it, dispute it or retract it.

00:02:06.833 --> 00:02:08.267
Each decision rescores the account,

00:02:08.267 --> 00:02:12.600
and any reaction held back is
released once. Or ask your agent:

00:02:12.600 --> 00:02:16.200
"List signals awaiting review
and verify the funding ones".

00:02:16.233 --> 00:02:19.567
The scan runs daily over your
target accounts through looot,

00:02:19.567 --> 00:02:20.733
inside a small spend cap per run.

00:02:20.733 --> 00:02:24.433
In the console: CRM, Signals
shows the status of the last run,

00:02:24.433 --> 00:02:26.067
and an owner can run it now.

00:02:26.067 --> 00:02:29.567
Or ask your agent: "Run the signal
scan now and tell me how it went".

00:02:29.567 --> 00:02:32.433
If looot isn't connected,
the scan says so and skips.

00:02:32.433 --> 00:02:34.133
In Dry Mode nothing is queued,

00:02:34.133 --> 00:02:37.567
and you can switch the scan off
under Settings, Feature flags.

00:02:37.633 --> 00:02:38.833
Here's where people slip.

00:02:38.833 --> 00:02:40.833
Web search results in the scan aren't

00:02:40.833 --> 00:02:43.300
yet checked as being
about the right account.

00:02:43.300 --> 00:02:46.833
A page can mention a company with a
similar name. Two things protect you.

00:02:46.833 --> 00:02:49.933
Set up a news binding, so
results come from a news source.

00:02:49.933 --> 00:02:51.633
And keep the gate on Strict,

00:02:51.633 --> 00:02:54.933
so a person confirms third
party signals before they count.

00:02:54.967 --> 00:02:58.400
To customize, change the signals
key of the scoring model: weights,

00:02:58.400 --> 00:03:01.367
half life, classes and auto verify rules.

00:03:01.367 --> 00:03:04.033
It goes through a change set,
and a different person signs.

00:03:04.033 --> 00:03:08.100
Advanced move: write auto verify
rules by kind, provider or party tier,

00:03:08.100 --> 00:03:10.133
so first party signals
never wait in the queue.

00:03:10.133 --> 00:03:11.467
And when one signal is wrong,

00:03:11.467 --> 00:03:14.767
ask your agent to retract
it and explain what changes.

00:03:14.800 --> 00:03:16.233
It improves from your decisions.

00:03:16.233 --> 00:03:21.267
Every verify, dispute and retract is
feedback: the account rescores at once.

00:03:21.267 --> 00:03:24.500
Once you trust a source, an auto
verify rule means less queue work.

00:03:24.500 --> 00:03:28.867
Score's Learning measures lift per
criterion, including your signal rules,

00:03:28.867 --> 00:03:31.667
and proposes weights a person approves.

00:03:31.667 --> 00:03:35.200
On the dashboard, watch hot and
warm accounts, the surge report,

00:03:35.200 --> 00:03:36.600
and signals awaiting review.

00:03:36.667 --> 00:03:39.133
Signals feed Score directly. Funding,

00:03:39.133 --> 00:03:42.433
hiring and intent signal
plays enrol one person

00:03:42.433 --> 00:03:45.833
per signal into an approved
sequence in Outreach,

00:03:45.833 --> 00:03:47.400
inside a daily cap.

00:03:47.400 --> 00:03:51.633
And Routing reacts to a new signal,
so the right owner hears first.

00:03:51.700 --> 00:03:55.200
Know the boundary: a live
provider for market events,

00:03:55.200 --> 00:03:58.633
and the account check
on web search results.

00:03:58.633 --> 00:04:03.100
Until then, the gate and the
review queue are your protection.

00:04:03.133 --> 00:04:07.333
Say it out loud: a Strict gate
means a queue that buries my team.

00:04:07.333 --> 00:04:10.800
Your own systems' server side
signals are verified automatically,

00:04:10.800 --> 00:04:14.100
and auto verify rules clear
the sources you trust.

00:04:14.100 --> 00:04:18.000
What waits is third party. That's
the part that needs a human eye.

00:04:18.033 --> 00:04:22.267
Boiled down: Signals come from
your systems and the outside world,

00:04:22.267 --> 00:04:27.733
each weighed by class, age and verification. The gate decides what counts.

00:04:27.733 --> 00:04:30.700
Hear everything. Count
only what's verified.

00:04:30.767 --> 00:04:34.433
You hear the market first, and
only verified signals count.

00:04:34.433 --> 00:04:39.467
Clear the Review queue under
CRM, Signals. Next up: Routing,

00:04:39.467 --> 00:04:43.100
which puts every qualified account
in front of the right owner.
